Backport of vllm-project/vllm#51478 onto vLLM v0.23.0.

    [Frontend] Support raw multimodal content in /inference/v1/generate
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/51478
    Merged upstream 2026-08-11, after the v0.23.0 tag.

Adds `content_parts` so one request can carry caller-supplied token ids together
with raw images/audio/video. Without it the only multimodal route that accepts an
authoritative prompt is /render -> /generate, which returns placeholder offsets
relative to a separately rendered sequence and forces the caller to remap them.

Python frontend only. AReaL launches vLLM through
areal.engine.vllm_ext.areal_vllm_server, which imports Python vLLM's run_server and
monkey-patches its Python build_app, so the Rust frontend is not on this path. A
Rust-fronted or externally managed server must carry #51478's Rust half instead;
AReaL's startup canary rejects an unpatched frontend rather than assuming it works.

Adapted rather than cherry-picked: upstream has since moved these modules under
scale_out/token_in_token_out, and v0.23.0 reaches the renderer through
self.openai_serving_render.renderer rather than self.online_renderer.renderer.
The unsupported-part-type branch is an addition, so an unrecognised type fails
loudly instead of being dropped from the prompt.

Delete this patch when the pinned vLLM release contains #51478.

diff --git a/vllm/entrypoints/serve/disagg/protocol.py b/vllm/entrypoints/serve/disagg/protocol.py
index 60d2a64..a01977c 100644
--- a/vllm/entrypoints/serve/disagg/protocol.py
+++ b/vllm/entrypoints/serve/disagg/protocol.py
@@ -81,6 +81,16 @@ class GenerateRequest(BaseModel):
     features: MultiModalFeatures | None = None
     """Multimodal hashes and placeholder positions (populated for MM inputs)."""
 
+    content_parts: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None
+    """Raw multimodal input; server resolves media. Mutually exclusive
+    with ``features``."""
+
+    @model_validator(mode="after")
+    def _check_mm_fields_exclusive(self) -> "GenerateRequest":
+        if self.content_parts and self.features:
+            raise ValueError("content_parts and features are mutually exclusive")
+        return self
+
     sampling_params: SamplingParams
     """The sampling parameters for the model."""
 
